The Collections Ontology
------------------------

src/collections/schema/collections.yaml, src/collections_linkml/datamodel/
and project/ render the Collections Ontology (CO) 2.0 by Paolo Ciccarese
and Silvio Peroni, http://purl.org/co, which they describe in "The
Collections Ontology: creating and handling collections in OWL 2 DL
frameworks", Semantic Web 5(6), 2014, https://doi.org/10.3233/SW-130121.
The schema keeps CO's names and IRIs. Its descriptions are this
project's own words, and its use does not imply endorsement by CO's
authors.

src/collections/schema/upstream/collections.owl is CO 2.0's OWL file,
unchanged, from
https://github.com/collections-ontology/collections-ontology at commit
619e7b02646321174635fd04be658e338bf7d1d7 (git object
4e19e4892212de2b1805923a7a69fa4ba8c1b424), read on 2026-10-31. That
repository is an export of the project's Google Code site and states no
licence of its own. The Google Code archive's record of the project,
https://code.google.com/archive/p/collections-ontology, gives its
licences. Its code, the files of its Subversion repository, is under the
Apache License, Version 2.0. Its other content, such as its wiki, is
under Creative Commons Attribution 3.0
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/). collections.owl is in that repository's trunk, so this
repository copies it under the Apache License, with this credit. The
schema cites one page of the wiki for a fact and copies none of its
text. The file differs from the copy in the archived Subversion trunk in
one line, the address of the error ontology it imports, which Silvio
Peroni changed on GitHub in 2019.

src/collections/schema/upstream/alignment.owl is CO's alignment file,
unchanged, from the same commit (git object
f6d6457b9b323e3e4bdf54ffeec5bc59f878f7ac), read on 2026-10-31. It is the
same file as in the archived Subversion trunk, so this repository copies
it under the Apache License, with the same credit. The schema's mappings
follow it.

